  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Periods of rain and breezy conditions from \nIsaias arrive Saturday night and continue through Sunday \n\nDeparting high pressure will maintain dry weather tonight and\nSaturday with increasing mid and high clouds. While clouds could\nmodulate min temps to some extent, expect another chilly night \nacross the northern tier with patchy frost possible. \n\nRain associated with Isaias is projected to reach the Laurel\nHighlands after midnight early Sunday morning and gradually\nexpand throughout central PA Sunday morning. Periods of rain\ncontinue Sunday afternoon into Sunday night before tapering off\nby early Monday. Total rainfall amounts are still forecast\nbetween 0.50 and 1.50 inches over a 24-36hr duration with a low\nrisk of potential flooding impacts. As post-tropical/TD Isaias\ntracks from the TN Valley into WV, it's wind field will bring \nbreezy conditions with max wind gusts 35-40 mph fcst over the \nridgetops in the Laurel Highlands on Sunday.",
